IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wills-dates`

-- Wills Act 1997 (Vic) -- the rules a will-maker, and a person with an interest in a deceased person's estate, meet:
-- who may make a will (ss 5, 6, 20), executing it (ss 7, 8A, 10, 11, 17), altering, revoking and reviving it (ss 12-16),
-- remuneration clauses (s 49A), Court-authorised wills for persons without testamentary capacity (ss 21, 21B, 21C, 24, 25),
-- informal wills (s 9), rectification (ss 31, 32), what becomes of a gift to a beneficiary who dies before or soon after
-- the will-maker (ss 35, 39, 45, 46(3)), the domestic partner definition (s 3), and who may see a will (s 50).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in wills-seat.l4 (the will-maker) and wills-seat-family.l4 (the
-- person with an interest in a deceased person's estate), which IMPORT it and never restate a rule. Nothing here is
-- exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("is not valid", "is not valid
-- unless", "is not effective unless", "may not be revoked except", "is void unless", "must not make an order", "does not
-- apply", an "if", "where" or "unless" condition that fails); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given,
-- with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The Court's and the Registrar's judgments ("satisfied", "thinks ... necessary", "in the
-- opinion of the Court") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them. Forks (Fn) are listed in
-- NOTES.md.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Wills Act 1997,
-- Version No. 036 (26 April 2021), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the authority of the
-- Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with the Copyright Act 1968
-- (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Wills Act 1997 -- the rules for the will-maker and the family`

§§ `Answers that combine`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a no` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN JUST v THEN (NOT v)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a yes` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN JUST v THEN v
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

§§ `Part 1 -- definitions (s 3)`

-- s 3(1): "minor means a person who is less than 18 years old".
GIVEN `the age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- a minor` `the age in years` IF `the age in years` LESS THAN 18

-- s 3(1): "domestic partner of a deceased person means -- (a) a person who was at the date of death in a registered
-- relationship with the person; or (b) a person to whom the person was not married but with whom the deceased person was
-- living at the date of death as a couple on a genuine domestic basis (irrespective of gender)". s 3(1A): "registered
-- relationship" has the Relationships Act 2008 meaning (borrowed, asked as a fact); for (b) "all the circumstances of their
-- relationship are to be taken into account" (a judgment, asked as a fact). A "means" definition: JUST FALSE when neither
-- limb holds.
GIVEN `in a registered relationship with the deceased at the date of death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `married to the deceased at the date of death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `living with the deceased as a couple on a genuine domestic basis at the date of death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3 -- the domestic partner of the deceased` `in a registered relationship with the deceased at the date of death` `married to the deceased at the date of death` `living with the deceased as a couple on a genuine domestic basis at the date of death` MEANS
    IF `in a registered relationship with the deceased at the date of death`
       OR (    (NOT `married to the deceased at the date of death`)
           AND `living with the deceased as a couple on a genuine domestic basis at the date of death`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 2 Division 1 -- who may make a will (ss 5, 6) and Part 3 Division 1 (s 20)`

DECLARE `Marital status` IS ONE OF
    `never married`
    `married now`
    `married before, but not now (divorced or widowed)`

DECLARE `Whether my will is valid as to my age` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I am 18 or over`
    `yes: the Court authorised it by an order under s 20`
    `yes: I am a married minor (s 6(b))`
    `yes, but it has no effect if the marriage I contemplate does not take place (s 6(a))`
    `no: a will made by a minor is not valid (s 5)`

-- s 5: "A will made by a minor is not valid." s 6: "Despite section 5 -- (a) a minor may make a will in contemplation of
-- marriage, and may alter or revoke such a will, but the will is of no effect if the marriage contemplated does not take
-- place; (b) a minor who is married may make, alter or revoke a will; (c) a minor who has been married may revoke the whole
-- or any part of a will made while the person was married or in contemplation of that marriage." s 20(1): "Despite section
-- 5, the Court may make an order under this section authorising a minor to make a will in specific terms or revoke a will."
-- The age is the age when the will is made. Testamentary capacity (soundness of mind) is common law, not in the Act: out.
GIVEN `my age when I make it` IS A NUMBER
      `my marital status` IS A `Marital status`
      `I make it in contemplation of a marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has authorised it by order under s 20` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether my will is valid as to my age`
`ss 5, 6, 20 -- my will is valid as to my age` `my age when I make it` `my marital status` `I make it in contemplation of a marriage` `the Court has authorised it by order under s 20` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `s 3 -- a minor` `my age when I make it` THEN `yes: I am 18 or over`
           IF `the Court has authorised it by order under s 20` THEN `yes: the Court authorised it by an order under s 20`
           IF `my marital status` EQUALS `married now` THEN `yes: I am a married minor (s 6(b))`
           IF `I make it in contemplation of a marriage` THEN `yes, but it has no effect if the marriage I contemplate does not take place (s 6(a))`
           OTHERWISE `no: a will made by a minor is not valid (s 5)`

-- Revoking as a minor. s 6(a) (a will made in contemplation of marriage), 6(b) (a married minor), 6(c) (a minor who has
-- been married, for a will made while married or in contemplation of that marriage), s 20 (a Court order). s 5 speaks only
-- of making a will; for any other minor the Act is silent (fork F1).
GIVEN `my age now` IS A NUMBER
      `my marital status` IS A `Marital status`
      `the will was made in contemplation of a marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will was made while I was married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has authorised the revocation by order under s 20` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 6, 20 -- I may revoke my will although a minor` `my age now` `my marital status` `the will was made in contemplation of a marriage` `the will was made while I was married` `the Court has authorised the revocation by order under s 20` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `s 3 -- a minor` `my age now` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the Court has authorised the revocation by order under s 20` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `my marital status` EQUALS `married now` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the will was made in contemplation of a marriage` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `my marital status` EQUALS `married before, but not now (divorced or widowed)` AND `the will was made while I was married` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 5 invalidates a minor's will, it does not speak of revoking; s 6 grants revocation to the minors it names; fork F1)

-- s 20(5): "Before making an order under this section, the Court must be satisfied that -- (a) the minor understands the
-- nature and effect of the proposed will or revocation and the extent of the property disposed of by it; and (b) the
-- proposed will or revocation accurately reflects the intentions of the minor; and (c) it is reasonable in all the
-- circumstances that the order should be made." (2): on the application of the minor or a person on behalf of the minor.
-- "must be satisfied" before the order: when any limb is not met, the answer is JUST FALSE. For a person of 18 or over the
-- section has nothing to do (a scope limit: NOTHING).
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `the Court is satisfied I understand the will and the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied it accurately reflects my intentions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied the order is reasonable in all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20 -- the Court may authorise my will as a minor` `my age` `the Court is satisfied I understand the will and the property` `the Court is satisfied it accurately reflects my intentions` `the Court is satisfied the order is reasonable in all the circumstances` MEANS
    IF NOT `s 3 -- a minor` `my age`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 20 speaks only of a minor; an adult needs no order)
    ELSE IF     `the Court is satisfied I understand the will and the property`
            AND `the Court is satisfied it accurately reflects my intentions`
            AND `the Court is satisfied the order is reasonable in all the circumstances`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 2 Divisions 2 and 4 -- executing and witnessing a will (ss 7, 8, 10, 11)`

DECLARE `Who signed the will` IS ONE OF
    `I signed it myself`
    `someone else signed it, in my presence and at my direction`
    `someone else signed it, but not in my presence or not at my direction`
    `nobody signed it`

-- s 7(1): "A will is not valid unless -- (a) it is in writing, and signed by the testator or by some other person, in the
-- presence of, and at the direction of the testator; and (b) the signature is made with the testator's intention of
-- executing a will, whether or not the signature appears at the foot of the will; and (c) the signature is made or
-- acknowledged by the testator in the presence of two or more witnesses present at the same time; and (d) at least two of the
-- witnesses attest and sign the will in the presence of the testator but not necessarily in the presence of each other."
-- s 10(1): "A person who is unable to see and attest that a testator has signed a document, may not act as a witness to a
-- will." So only witnesses able to see count (fork F2). s 8: a witness need not know it was a will. s 7(2): no attestation
-- clause is needed. "is not valid unless": JUST FALSE when any limb fails.
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who signed` IS A `Who signed the will`
      `signed intending to execute a will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `witnesses able to see, present together when I signed or acknowledged my signature` IS A NUMBER
      `of them, how many then signed the will in my presence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(1), 10 -- my will is validly executed in person` `it is in writing` `who signed` `signed intending to execute a will` `witnesses able to see, present together when I signed or acknowledged my signature` `of them, how many then signed the will in my presence` MEANS
    IF     `it is in writing`
       AND `the signature is a proper one`
       AND `signed intending to execute a will`
       AND `witnesses able to see, present together when I signed or acknowledged my signature` AT LEAST 2
       AND `the attesting witnesses` AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the signature is a proper one` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who signed`
            WHEN `I signed it myself` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `someone else signed it, in my presence and at my direction` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `the attesting witnesses` MEANS
            IF `of them, how many then signed the will in my presence` GREATER THAN `witnesses able to see, present together when I signed or acknowledged my signature`
            THEN `witnesses able to see, present together when I signed or acknowledged my signature`
            ELSE `of them, how many then signed the will in my presence`

-- s 3(1): "special witness means -- (a) an Australian legal practitioner; or (b) a justice of the peace appointed under
-- section 7 of the Honorary Justices Act 2014; or (c) a person who is a member of a prescribed class of person". No class is
-- prescribed in a deposited instrument.
DECLARE `Kind of special witness` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian legal practitioner`
    `a justice of the peace`
    `a member of a prescribed class`
    `no special witness`

-- s 8A, with s 7(5)-(7) and s 19E(2). s 8A(2): one witness "must be a special witness"; (3) "All elements ... must be
-- carried out on the same day and within Victoria"; (4) the testator signs (or directs a substitute signatory) with all
-- witnesses clearly seeing the signature made, by audio visual link or a mix of presence and link; (5), (6) the physically
-- present witnesses sign, the special witness signs last; (7) the will is sent electronically to each witness on the link,
-- who must (a) be reasonably satisfied it is the same document, (b) put on it a statement that they witnessed it by audio
-- visual link under the procedure, (c) sign with the testator seeing; (d) the special witness must also check the will and
-- state that it was signed and witnessed under the procedure, what kind of special witness they are, and whether a recording
-- was made. s 7(5): a will so executed "is a valid will". s 19E(2): the procedure "cannot be used for international wills".
-- s 7(7): presence by audio visual link counts only "in accordance with the remote execution procedure", so a will that
-- misses a step of s 8A has no witnesses present in the s 7(1)(c) sense: JUST FALSE (fork F3, "a bare must not done").
-- s 8C: a recording is optional and does not affect validity.
GIVEN `it is an international will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special witness` IS A `Kind of special witness`
      `number of witnesses` IS A NUMBER
      `everything was done on the same day and within Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every witness clearly saw the signature being made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special witness signed last` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each witness on the link put on the statement and signed while I watched` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special witness checked the will and put on the special witness statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 7(5), 8A, 19E(2) -- my will is validly executed by the remote execution procedure` `it is an international will` `the special witness` `number of witnesses` `everything was done on the same day and within Victoria` `every witness clearly saw the signature being made` `the special witness signed last` `each witness on the link put on the statement and signed while I watched` `the special witness checked the will and put on the special witness statement` MEANS
    IF `it is an international will`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF     (NOT (`the special witness` EQUALS `no special witness`))
            AND `number of witnesses` AT LEAST 2
            AND `everything was done on the same day and within Victoria`
            AND `every witness clearly saw the signature being made`
            AND `the special witness signed last`
            AND `each witness on the link put on the statement and signed while I watched`
            AND `the special witness checked the will and put on the special witness statement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 11: "A person who witnesses a will or his or her spouse or domestic partner, at the time the will is witnessed, is not
-- disqualified from taking a benefit under the will." A flat negative of disqualification: the witness may take.
GIVEN `the witness or their spouse or partner is a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11 -- a witness who benefits keeps the gift` `the witness or their spouse or partner is a beneficiary` MEANS
    IF `the witness or their spouse or partner is a beneficiary`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 11 speaks only of a witness, or the witness's spouse or partner, who takes a benefit)

§§ `Part 2 Division 6 -- a will executed outside Victoria (s 17)`

-- s 17(1): "A will is to be taken to be properly executed if its execution conforms to the internal law in force in the
-- place -- (a) where it was executed; or (b) which was the testator's domicile or habitual residence, either at the time the
-- will was executed, or at the testator's death; or (c) of which the testator was a national, either at the date of execution
-- of the will, or at the testator's death." s 17(2)(b): a will, so far as it disposes of immovable property, executed under
-- the law of the place where the property is. Whether the execution conforms to a foreign law is asked as a fact. When none
-- holds, s 17 is silent (s 7 may still be met): NOTHING.
GIVEN `conforms to the law of the place where it was executed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `conforms to the law of my domicile or habitual residence, when made or at death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `conforms to the law of a country I was a national of, when made or at death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for land, conforms to the law of the place where the land is` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 -- my will is taken to be properly executed under a foreign law` `conforms to the law of the place where it was executed` `conforms to the law of my domicile or habitual residence, when made or at death` `conforms to the law of a country I was a national of, when made or at death` `for land, conforms to the law of the place where the land is` MEANS
    IF    `conforms to the law of the place where it was executed`
       OR `conforms to the law of my domicile or habitual residence, when made or at death`
       OR `conforms to the law of a country I was a national of, when made or at death`
       OR `for land, conforms to the law of the place where the land is`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 17 says when a will is taken to be properly executed, not when it is not; s 7 may still be met)

§§ `Part 2 Division 5 -- revocation (ss 12, 13, 14)`

DECLARE `How I tried to revoke the will` IS ONE OF
    `by a later will`
    `by a writing declaring that I revoke it`
    `by burning, tearing or otherwise destroying it`
    `by writing on it or otherwise dealing with it`
    `in some other way (telling someone, or a writing not signed and witnessed)`

DECLARE `Who did the act of revoking` IS ONE OF
    `I did`
    `someone else, in my presence and at my direction`
    `someone else, not in my presence or not at my direction`

-- s 12(2): "Subject to -- (b) sections 13 and 14; and (c) any order made by the Court under this Act authorising the
-- revocation of a will; and (d) any order made by the Court under this Act dispensing with the formal requirements for
-- revoking a will -- the whole or any part of a will may not be revoked except -- (da) by a later will; or (e) by some
-- writing, declaring an intention to revoke it, executed in the manner in which a will is required to be executed by this
-- Act; or (f) by the testator, or some person in his or her presence and by his or her direction, burning, tearing or
-- otherwise destroying the will with the intention of revoking it; or (g) by the testator, or by some person in his or her
-- presence and at his or her direction, writing on the will or dealing with the will in such a manner that the Court is
-- satisfied, from the state of the will, that the testator intended to revoke it." A closed list ("may not ... except"):
-- JUST FALSE outside it. Whether a later will revokes the earlier one (by an express clause or by inconsistency) is not
-- said by the Act; it is asked as a fact (fork F4). s 12(3): (e) may use the remote execution procedure. The Court's power
-- after death (s 9(2)) is in the family seat.
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I tried to revoke the will`
      `the later will or writing was signed and witnessed as a will must be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later will revokes it, expressly or by being inconsistent with it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who did it` IS A `Who did the act of revoking`
      `it was done intending to revoke the will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied from the state of the will that I intended to revoke it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12 -- my will is revoked by what I did` `how` `the later will or writing was signed and witnessed as a will must be` `the later will revokes it, expressly or by being inconsistent with it` `who did it` `it was done intending to revoke the will` `the Court is satisfied from the state of the will that I intended to revoke it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `by a later will` THEN
        IF `the later will or writing was signed and witnessed as a will must be` AND `the later will revokes it, expressly or by being inconsistent with it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `by a writing declaring that I revoke it` THEN
        IF `the later will or writing was signed and witnessed as a will must be` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `by burning, tearing or otherwise destroying it` THEN
        IF `done by me or at my direction in my presence` AND `it was done intending to revoke the will`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `by writing on it or otherwise dealing with it` THEN
        IF `done by me or at my direction in my presence` AND `the Court is satisfied from the state of the will that I intended to revoke it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `in some other way (telling someone, or a writing not signed and witnessed)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `done by me or at my direction in my presence` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who did it`
            WHEN `I did` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `someone else, in my presence and at my direction` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `A new relationship since the will` IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `I married`
    `I began a domestic relationship (registered, or living together as a couple) without marrying`

DECLARE `What the new relationship does to my will` IS ONE OF
    `nothing: there has been no marriage since the will was made`
    `nothing: only a marriage revokes a will, not a domestic relationship (ss 12, 13)`
    `nothing: the will was made in contemplation of this marriage (s 13(3)(a))`
    `nothing: the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally (s 13(3)(b))`
    `the will is revoked, except gifts to and appointments of the person I am married to at my death, and the powers s 13(2)(c) saves`

-- s 13(1): "A will is revoked by the marriage of the testator." (2): not revoked by the marriage: "(a) a disposition to the
-- person to whom the testator is married at the time of his or her death; or (b) an appointment as executor, trustee,
-- advisory trustee or guardian of the person to whom the testator is married at the time of his or her death; or (c) a power
-- to exercise, by will, a power of appointment, when, if the testator did not exercise the power, the property so appointed
-- would not pass to the executor or administrator or the State Trustees under section 19 of the Administration and Probate
-- Act 1958". (3): "(a) a will made in contemplation of a marriage (whether or not that contemplation is expressed in the
-- will) is not revoked by the solemnisation of the marriage contemplated; and (b) a will which is expressed to be made in
-- contemplation of marriage generally is not revoked by the marriage of the testator." A domestic relationship is not a
-- marriage, and s 12(2) closes the list of ways a will is revoked: a domestic relationship revokes nothing (finding 2).
-- s 16(4): a revived will is "taken to have been executed on the date on which the will is revived"; "since the will" counts
-- from that date.
GIVEN `the new relationship` IS A `A new relationship since the will`
      `the will was made in contemplation of this marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What the new relationship does to my will`
`ss 12, 13 -- what my marriage or new relationship does to my will` `the new relationship` `the will was made in contemplation of this marriage` `the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the new relationship`
    WHEN `none` THEN `nothing: there has been no marriage since the will was made`
    WHEN `I began a domestic relationship (registered, or living together as a couple) without marrying` THEN `nothing: only a marriage revokes a will, not a domestic relationship (ss 12, 13)`
    WHEN `I married` THEN
        BRANCH IF `the will was made in contemplation of this marriage` THEN `nothing: the will was made in contemplation of this marriage (s 13(3)(a))`
               IF `the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally` THEN `nothing: the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally (s 13(3)(b))`
               OTHERWISE `the will is revoked, except gifts to and appointments of the person I am married to at my death, and the powers s 13(2)(c) saves`

DECLARE `How the relationship ended` IS ONE OF
    `a divorce under the Family Law Act 1975 took effect`
    `the Family Court annulled the marriage`
    `the marriage was dissolved or annulled overseas, in a way recognised in Australia`
    `we separated, but there is no divorce or annulment`
    `a domestic relationship (not a marriage) ended`

DECLARE `Part of my will that names my former spouse` IS ONE OF
    `a gift to my former spouse`
    `my former spouse as executor`
    `my former spouse as trustee`
    `my former spouse as trustee of property left on trust for beneficiaries who include their children`
    `my former spouse as advisory trustee or guardian`
    `a power of appointment exercisable by or in favour of my former spouse`
    `a power of appointment exercisable by my former spouse only in favour of our children`

-- s 14(1): "The divorce of a testator revokes -- (a) any disposition to the divorced spouse of the testator, made in a will in
-- existence at the time of the divorce; and (b) the grant of a power of appointment by the will exercisable by or in favour of
-- the spouse, other than a power of appointment exercisable by the spouse only in favour of persons who are the children of
-- both the testator and the spouse; and (c) any appointment made by the will of the spouse as an executor, trustee, advisory
-- trustee or guardian other than the appointment of the spouse as a trustee of property left by the will upon trust for
-- beneficiaries that include the children of the spouse." (2): "This section does not apply to any disposition, appointment
-- or grant, if it appears that the testator did not want the disposition, appointment or grant to be revoked upon the ending
-- of the marriage." (3): the will takes effect "as if the spouse had predeceased the testator". (4): "divorce means the
-- ending of a marriage by -- (a) a decree of dissolution of the marriage becoming absolute under the Family Law Act 1975 ...;
-- (b) the granting of a decree of nullity ... by the Family Court of Australia; or (c) the dissolution or annulment ... in
-- accordance with the law of a place outside Australia, if ... recognised in Australia". "spouse includes a party to a
-- purported or void marriage." Outside s 14, s 12(2) closes the ways a will is revoked: separation alone, the end of a
-- domestic relationship, the "other than" parts, and parts the testator wanted kept are not revoked: JUST FALSE (fork F5
-- for "other than"; finding 3 for the Act's out-of-date names).
GIVEN `the ending` IS A `How the relationship ended`
      `the will existed at the time of the divorce` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part` IS A `Part of my will that names my former spouse`
      `it appears I did not want it revoked when the marriage ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 12, 14 -- my divorce revokes this part of my will` `the ending` `the will existed at the time of the divorce` `the part` `it appears I did not want it revoked when the marriage ended` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `a divorce within s 14(4)` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF NOT `the will existed at the time of the divorce` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `it appears I did not want it revoked when the marriage ended` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `the part`
               WHEN `my former spouse as trustee of property left on trust for beneficiaries who include their children` THEN JUST FALSE
               WHEN `a power of appointment exercisable by my former spouse only in favour of our children` THEN JUST FALSE
               OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `a divorce within s 14(4)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the ending`
            WHEN `a divorce under the Family Law Act 1975 took effect` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the Family Court annulled the marriage` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the marriage was dissolved or annulled overseas, in a way recognised in Australia` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Part 2 Division 5 -- altering and reviving a will (ss 15, 16)`

-- s 15(1): "An alteration to a will after it has been executed is not effective unless the alteration is executed in the
-- manner in which the will is required to be executed under this Act." (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply to an alteration
-- to a will if the words or effect of the will are no longer apparent because of the alteration." (3): signatures in the
-- margin or beside the alteration, or authenticating a memorandum on the will, suffice. (4), (5): the remote execution
-- procedure and electronic signatures may be used. An alteration made before execution is common law: NOTHING. An
-- obliteration (2) is outside s 15(1); whether it revokes that part is s 12(2)(g): NOTHING here (fork F6).
GIVEN `made after the will was executed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alteration was signed by me and witnessed as a will must be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the original words can no longer be made out because of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 -- my alteration is effective` `made after the will was executed` `the alteration was signed by me and witnessed as a will must be` `the original words can no longer be made out because of it` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `made after the will was executed` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 15 speaks only of an alteration after execution)
           IF `the alteration was signed by me and witnessed as a will must be` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the original words can no longer be made out because of it` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 15(2) disapplies s 15(1) for an obliteration and says no more; fork F6)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `What revives my revoked will` IS ONE OF
    `the will is revived (s 16(1))`
    `only the part most recently revoked is revived (s 16(2))`
    `the Act does not revive it on these facts`

-- s 16(1): "A will or part of a will which has been revoked is revived by re-execution or by execution of a codicil which
-- shows an intention to revive the will or part." (2): "A revival of a will which was partly revoked and later revoked as
-- to the balance only revives that part of the will most recently revoked." (3): not if "a contrary intention appears in
-- the document which revives the will". (4): the revived will is "taken to have been executed on the date on which the will
-- is revived". s 16(1) does not say "only": when neither way is used the Act is silent (NOTHING-kind, given as the third
-- constructor).
GIVEN `I re-executed it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I executed a codicil showing an intention to revive it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was partly revoked and later revoked as to the rest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reviving document shows a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What revives my revoked will`
`s 16 -- what revives my revoked will` `I re-executed it` `I executed a codicil showing an intention to revive it` `it was partly revoked and later revoked as to the rest` `the reviving document shows a contrary intention` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`I re-executed it` OR `I executed a codicil showing an intention to revive it`) THEN `the Act does not revive it on these facts`
           IF `it was partly revoked and later revoked as to the rest` AND NOT `the reviving document shows a contrary intention` THEN `only the part most recently revoked is revived (s 16(2))`
           OTHERWISE `the will is revived (s 16(1))`

§§ `Part 4 -- remuneration clauses (s 49A)`

-- s 49A: "A remuneration clause in a will is void unless -- (a) the testator gave written informed consent to the inclusion
-- of the remuneration clause; and (b) that written informed consent was given by the testator before the will was executed."
-- s 56: "Section 49A only applies to a will executed on or after the commencement of that section." The commencement, 1
-- November 2017, is read from the deposited endnotes (No. 41/2017 ss 28-30 "on 1.11.17"), which do not form part of the Act.
-- "remuneration clause" is borrowed from the Administration and Probate Act 1958 (a clause letting an executor charge),
-- asked as a fact.
`s 56 -- the day section 49A commenced` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 11 2017

GIVEN `the day the will was executed` IS A DATE
      `I gave written informed consent to the clause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave it before the will was executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49A -- the remuneration clause in my will is not void` `the day the will was executed` `I gave written informed consent to the clause` `I gave it before the will was executed` MEANS
    IF `the days from` `s 56 -- the day section 49A commenced` `to` `the day the will was executed` LESS THAN 0
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 56 confines s 49A to wills executed on or after 1 November 2017; the general law answers)
    ELSE IF `I gave written informed consent to the clause` AND `I gave it before the will was executed`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 3 Division 2 -- Court-authorised wills for a person without testamentary capacity (ss 21-25)`

-- s 21(1): the Court may authorise a will "to be made in specific terms approved by the Court or revoked on behalf of a
-- person who does not have testamentary capacity". (2): "Any person may make an application". (3): "... must not make an
-- order under this section on behalf of a person who is deceased at the time the order is made." s 21B: "Before making an
-- order under section 21, the Court must be satisfied that -- (a) the person ... does not have testamentary capacity; and
-- (b) the proposed will or revocation reflects what the intentions of the person would be likely to be, or what the
-- intentions of the person might reasonably be expected to be, if the person had testamentary capacity; and (c) it is
-- reasonable in all the circumstances for the Court, by order, to authorise the making of the will for the person."
GIVEN `the person is alive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied the person lacks testamentary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied the proposed will reflects their likely intentions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied the order is reasonable in all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 21, 21B -- the Court may authorise a will for the person` `the person is alive` `the Court is satisfied the person lacks testamentary capacity` `the Court is satisfied the proposed will reflects their likely intentions` `the Court is satisfied the order is reasonable in all the circumstances` MEANS
    IF     `the person is alive`
       AND `the Court is satisfied the person lacks testamentary capacity`
       AND `the Court is satisfied the proposed will reflects their likely intentions`
       AND `the Court is satisfied the order is reasonable in all the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `My role in a statutory will application` IS ONE OF
    `I am the person the will is for`
    `I am the person's lawyer`
    `I am the person's attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
    `I am the person's guardian or administrator under the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019`
    `the Court considers I have a genuine interest in the matter`
    `none of these`

-- s 21C: "Each of the following persons is entitled to appear and be heard ... -- (a) the person on whose behalf the will is
-- to be made; (b) an Australian legal practitioner representing that person; (c) an attorney appointed by that person under
-- an enduring power of attorney; (d) any guardian or administrator for the person appointed under the Guardianship and
-- Administration Act 2019; (e) any other person who has, in the opinion of the Court, a genuine interest in the matter."
-- A list of who is entitled, not closed with "only": outside it, NOTHING.
GIVEN `my role` IS A `My role in a statutory will application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21C -- I am entitled to appear and be heard` `my role` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (listed without closing the list: s 21C names who is entitled, not who is barred)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 25(1): "A will which is made under an order under section 21 is not valid unless it is in writing, signed by the
-- Registrar and sealed with the seal of the Court." (2): the same for a revocation. (5): failing to deposit it with the
-- Registrar does not affect validity.
GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `signed by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sealed with the seal of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25 -- the Court-authorised will is valid` `in writing` `signed by the Registrar` `sealed with the seal of the Court` MEANS
    IF `in writing` AND `signed by the Registrar` AND `sealed with the seal of the Court` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 24: "If a will has been made under an order under section 21 on behalf of a person who acquires or regains testamentary
-- capacity after the making of the order, that person may revoke or deal with the will without an order under section 21."
GIVEN `I have acquired or regained testamentary capacity since the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24 -- I may revoke or change my Court-authorised will myself` `I have acquired or regained testamentary capacity since the order` MEANS
    IF `I have acquired or regained testamentary capacity since the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 24 speaks only of a person who has regained capacity; otherwise a further order under s 21)

§§ `Part 2 Division 3 -- informal wills: the Court's power to dispense (s 9)`

DECLARE `What was not properly executed` IS ONE OF
    `nothing: it was executed as the Act requires`
    `the whole document`
    `an alteration to the will`

DECLARE `Whether the Court may admit the document` IS ONE OF
    `no need: the document is executed as the Act requires`
    `the Court may admit it to probate as the will (s 9(1))`
    `s 9 gives the Court no power on these facts: it is not satisfied the deceased intended it as their will`

-- s 9(1): "The Supreme Court may admit to probate as the will of a deceased person -- (a) a document which has not been
-- executed in the manner in which a will is required to be executed by this Act; or (b) a document, an alteration to which
-- has not been executed in the manner in which an alteration to a will is required to be executed by this Act -- if the
-- Court is satisfied that that person intended the document to be his or her will." (3): the Court may have regard to
-- evidence of the manner of execution and of the testator's testamentary intentions, including statements. (4): it applies
-- to a document made within or outside the State. (6): "document" has the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 meaning
-- (wide: includes electronic records; borrowed). "if the Court is satisfied": JUST FALSE-kind when not.
GIVEN `what` IS A `What was not properly executed`
      `the Court is satisfied the deceased intended the document to be their will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether the Court may admit the document`
`s 9(1) -- the Court may admit the informal document as the will` `what` `the Court is satisfied the deceased intended the document to be their will` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `nothing: it was executed as the Act requires` THEN `no need: the document is executed as the Act requires`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the Court is satisfied the deceased intended the document to be their will`
        THEN `the Court may admit it to probate as the will (s 9(1))`
        ELSE `s 9 gives the Court no power on these facts: it is not satisfied the deceased intended it as their will`

-- s 9(2): "The Supreme Court may refuse to admit a will to probate which the testator has purported to revoke by some
-- writing, where the writing has not been executed in the manner in which a will is required to be executed by this Act, if
-- the Court is satisfied that the testator intended to revoke the will by that writing." A writing that was executed is
-- itself a revocation under s 12(2)(e); s 9(2) is not needed, and is outside its own wording: NOTHING.
GIVEN `the revoking writing was signed and witnessed as a will must be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied the deceased intended the writing to revoke the will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) -- the Court may refuse probate of a will revoked by an informal writing` `the revoking writing was signed and witnessed as a will must be` `the Court is satisfied the deceased intended the writing to revoke the will` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the revoking writing was signed and witnessed as a will must be` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 9(2) speaks of an unexecuted writing; an executed one revokes under s 12(2)(e))
           IF `the Court is satisfied the deceased intended the writing to revoke the will` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 9(5): "The Registrar may exercise the powers of the Court under this section -- (a) where the Court has authorised the
-- Registrar to exercise the Court's powers under this section; and (b) where -- (i) all persons who would be affected by a
-- decision under this section so consent; or (ii) if consent is not given, the value of the estate does not exceed the limit
-- set for the purposes of this section by the Court." The limit is set by the Court and is not in a deposited instrument:
-- an input. "where": JUST FALSE when it fails. "does not exceed": equal to the limit is within it.
GIVEN `the Court has authorised the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `everyone affected consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the estate` IS A NUMBER
      `the limit the Court has set` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(5) -- the Registrar may decide the informal will application` `the Court has authorised the Registrar` `everyone affected consents` `the value of the estate` `the limit the Court has set` MEANS
    IF     `the Court has authorised the Registrar`
       AND (`everyone affected consents` OR `the value of the estate` AT MOST `the limit the Court has set`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 3 Division 3 -- rectification (ss 31, 32)`

DECLARE `Why the will does not carry out the will-maker's intentions` IS ONE OF
    `a clerical error was made`
    `the will does not give effect to the will-maker's instructions`
    `some other reason (a change of mind, a mistake about the law or the effect of the words)`

-- s 31(1): "The Court may make an order to rectify a will to carry out the intentions of the testator, if the Court is
-- satisfied that the will does not carry out the testator's intentions because -- (a) a clerical error was made; or (b) the
-- will does not give effect to the testator's instructions." "if ... because": JUST FALSE for any other reason, and when the
-- Court is not satisfied. s 32: a certified copy of the order is attached to the grant.
GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Why the will does not carry out the will-maker's intentions`
      `the Court is satisfied the will does not carry out the intentions for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(1) -- the Court may rectify the will` `the reason` `the Court is satisfied the will does not carry out the intentions for that reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `some other reason (a change of mind, a mistake about the law or the effect of the words)` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the Court is satisfied the will does not carry out the intentions for that reason` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 31(2): "A person who wishes to make an application for an order under subsection (1) must apply to the Court within 6
-- months from the date of the grant of probate." The last day: six calendar months from the grant, the day of the grant
-- excluded (wills-dates.l4, fork F8). The duty is a regulative rule: DO apply WITHIN the days to that last day, counted from
-- the day of the grant (day 0), LEST BREACH. The "breach" is losing the right to apply without an extension, not a wrong.
-- (3): "The Court may extend the period of time for making an application if the Court thinks this is necessary, even if the
-- original period of time has expired, but not if the final distribution of the estate has been made."
DECLARE `Rectification party` IS ONE OF `the applicant`
DECLARE `Rectification act` IS ONE OF `apply to the Court for rectification`

GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 31(2) -- the last day to apply for rectification` `the day of the grant` MEANS `the last day of` 6 `months from` `the day of the grant`

GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 31(2) -- the days allowed to apply` `the day of the grant` MEANS
    `the days from` `the day of the grant` `to` (`s 31(2) -- the last day to apply for rectification` `the day of the grant`)

GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Rectification party` `Rectification act`
`s 31(2) -- apply for rectification within 6 months of the grant` `the day of the grant` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    DO `apply to the Court for rectification`
    WITHIN `s 31(2) -- the days allowed to apply` `the day of the grant`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "no application within 6 months from the date of the grant of probate: rectification only if the Court extends the period, and never after the final distribution (s 31(2), (3))"

-- The helper that runs the rule over what happened (the shape the County Court Act 1958 encoding uses). On the stable l4 a
-- CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the application was made, FULFILLED means in time and
-- anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether applying today would still be in time. It takes a DEONTIC
-- value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Rectification party` `Rectification act`
      `the time it was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is in time under` `the rule` `at` `the time it was made` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was made`), (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the Court for rectification` `the time it was made`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where my rectification application stands` IS ONE OF
    `no grant of probate yet: the six months have not begun`
    `made in time (s 31(2))`
    `still open: I can apply in time`
    `out of time, but the Court has extended the period (s 31(3))`
    `out of time: I need the Court to extend the period (s 31(3))`
    `out of time, and the Court cannot extend it: the estate has been finally distributed (s 31(3))`

GIVEN `probate has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
      `the Court has extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the estate has been finally distributed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where my rectification application stands`
`s 31(2), (3) -- where my rectification application stands` `probate has been granted` `the day of the grant` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today` `the Court has extended the period` `the estate has been finally distributed` MEANS
    IF NOT `probate has been granted`
    THEN `no grant of probate yet: the six months have not begun`
    ELSE IF `the application is in time under` (`s 31(2) -- apply for rectification within 6 months of the grant` `the day of the grant`) `at` `the time`
         THEN IF `I have applied` THEN `made in time (s 31(2))` ELSE `still open: I can apply in time`
         ELSE BRANCH IF `the Court has extended the period` THEN `out of time, but the Court has extended the period (s 31(3))`
                     IF `the estate has been finally distributed` THEN `out of time, and the Court cannot extend it: the estate has been finally distributed (s 31(3))`
                     OTHERWISE `out of time: I need the Court to extend the period (s 31(3))`
    WHERE
        `the time` MEANS
            IF `I have applied`
            THEN `the days from` `the day of the grant` `to` `the day I applied`
            ELSE `the days from` `the day of the grant` `to` `today`

§§ `Part 4 -- what becomes of a gift to a beneficiary who dies before, or soon after, the will-maker (ss 35, 39, 45, 46(3))`

-- s 39(1): "If a disposition is made to a person who dies within 30 days after the death of the testator, the will is to
-- take effect as if the person had died before the testator." (2): not "if a contrary intention appears in the will"; (3):
-- "A general requirement or condition that a beneficiary survive the testator is not a contrary intention".
-- Counting: the day of the will-maker's death is excluded; a beneficiary who dies on the 30th day after has died "within 30
-- days" and has not survived the will-maker "for thirty days" (s 45(1)(b)); one who dies on the 31st day has (fork F7).
GIVEN `the will-maker's death` IS A DATE
      `the beneficiary's death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 39, 45 -- the beneficiary did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` `the will-maker's death` `the beneficiary's death` IF
    `the days from` `the will-maker's death` `to` `the beneficiary's death` AT MOST 30

DECLARE `What becomes of the gift` IS ONE OF
    `the gift takes effect: the beneficiary survived the will-maker by 30 days`
    `the will's own terms decide: it shows a contrary intention (ss 35(2), 39(2), 45(3))`
    `the beneficiary's own issue who survive the will-maker by 30 days take the share (s 45(1))`
    `the failed share passes to the other shares of the residue proportionately (s 46(3))`
    `the gift falls into the residuary estate (s 35(1))`

-- s 45(1): "If a person makes a disposition to any of his or her issue, where -- (a) the disposition is not a disposition to
-- which section 43 applies; and (b) one or more of the issue do not survive the testator for thirty days; and (c) the
-- interest in the property is not determinable at or before the death of the issue -- the issue of the deceased issue who
-- survive the testator for 30 days take the deceased issue's share ...". (3): a contrary intention displaces it, but a
-- general survival or age condition is not one. (4): not where the original beneficiary "did not fulfil a contingency
-- required by the will". s 46(3): "If any part of -- (a) a residuary disposition which is in fractional parts; or (b) a
-- disposition of the whole of the estate which is in fractional parts -- fails, the part that fails passes to the part which
-- does not fail and, if there is more than one part which does not fail, to all those parts proportionately." (4): not if a
-- contrary intention appears. s 35(1): "If any disposition of property is ineffective, the will takes effect as if the
-- property were part of the residuary estate of the testator." (2): not if a contrary intention appears (in the will or
-- elsewhere). s 43 (gifts to "issue" as a class) and s 45(1)(c) (an interest ending at or before the issue's death) are
-- asked as one fact. One contrary-intention input stands for ss 35(2), 39(2), 45(3) and 46(4) (fork F9).
GIVEN `the beneficiary is still alive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will-maker's death` IS A DATE
      `the beneficiary's death` IS A DATE
      `the will shows a contrary intention, beyond a general condition to survive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary was the will-maker's child, grandchild or other issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary's own issue survived the will-maker by 30 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gift is to issue as a class, or the interest ends at the beneficiary's death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary had not met a condition the will required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gift is a fractional share of the residue or of the whole estate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What becomes of the gift`
`ss 35, 39, 45, 46 -- what becomes of the gift` `the beneficiary is still alive` `the will-maker's death` `the beneficiary's death` `the will shows a contrary intention, beyond a general condition to survive` `the beneficiary was the will-maker's child, grandchild or other issue` `the beneficiary's own issue survived the will-maker by 30 days` `the gift is to issue as a class, or the interest ends at the beneficiary's death` `the beneficiary had not met a condition the will required` `the gift is a fractional share of the residue or of the whole estate` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the beneficiary is still alive` THEN `the gift takes effect: the beneficiary survived the will-maker by 30 days`
           IF NOT `ss 39, 45 -- the beneficiary did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` `the will-maker's death` `the beneficiary's death` THEN `the gift takes effect: the beneficiary survived the will-maker by 30 days`
           IF `the will shows a contrary intention, beyond a general condition to survive` THEN `the will's own terms decide: it shows a contrary intention (ss 35(2), 39(2), 45(3))`
           IF     `the beneficiary was the will-maker's child, grandchild or other issue`
              AND `the beneficiary's own issue survived the will-maker by 30 days`
              AND (NOT `the gift is to issue as a class, or the interest ends at the beneficiary's death`)
              AND (NOT `the beneficiary had not met a condition the will required`)
              THEN `the beneficiary's own issue who survive the will-maker by 30 days take the share (s 45(1))`
           IF `the gift is a fractional share of the residue or of the whole estate` THEN `the failed share passes to the other shares of the residue proportionately (s 46(3))`
           OTHERWISE `the gift falls into the residuary estate (s 35(1))`

§§ `Part 5 -- who may see a will (s 50)`

DECLARE `Who I am to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `a person named or referred to in the will`
    `a beneficiary named in an earlier will`
    `the deceased's spouse at the date of death`
    `the deceased's domestic partner`
    `a parent, guardian or child of the deceased`
    `a person entitled to a share if the deceased had died without a will`
    `a parent or guardian of a minor named in the will or entitled on intestacy`
    `a creditor or other claimant against the estate, with evidence of the claim`
    `a creditor or other claimant against the estate, without evidence of the claim`
    `someone else`

-- s 50: "A person who has possession and control of a will, a revoked will or a purported will of a deceased person must
-- allow the following persons to inspect and make copies of the will (at their own expense) -- (a) any person named or
-- referred to in the will, whether as beneficiary or not; (b) any person named or referred to in any earlier will as a
-- beneficiary; (c) any spouse of the testator at the date of the testator's death; (d) any domestic partner of the testator;
-- (e) any parent, guardian or children of the deceased person; (f) any person who would be entitled to a share of the estate
-- if the deceased person had died intestate; (g) any parent or guardian of a minor referred to in the will or who would be
-- entitled to a share of the estate of the testator if the testator had died intestate; (h) any creditor or other person who
-- has a claim at law or in equity against the estate of the deceased person and who produces evidence of that claim." The
-- list is not closed with "only": outside it, NOTHING (the holder may still let others see it).
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am to the deceased`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50 -- I am entitled to inspect and copy the will` `who I am` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who I am`
    WHEN `a creditor or other claimant against the estate, without evidence of the claim` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: (h) reaches a claimant "who produces evidence of that claim")
    WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (listed without closing the list)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
